{"id": "EUVD-2026-91850", "enisaUuid": "b7be0f4a-4e0e-3477-afb7-425d1e0dd8c4", "description": "OpenLiteSpeed before 1.9.3 contains a local privilege escalation vulnerability in admin/misc/lsup.sh that runs unverified update packages from a nobody-writable directory as root. Attackers controlling the nobody web process can replace the package in /usr/local/lsws/autoupdate/ before extraction, so its install.sh runs as root on the next update.", "datePublished": "2026-10-02T23:28:45", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-05T14:50:08", "baseScore": 5.4, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:H/AT:P/PR:L/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://openlitespeed.org/release-log/version-1-9-x/", "https://github.com/litespeedtech/openlitespeed/commit/468523ce84388cea9ba6633c26517bc05b3e2bc1", "https://github.com/litespeedtech/openlitespeed/blob/v1.9.2/dist/admin/misc/lsup.sh#L538", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/openlitespeed-before-1.9.3-local-privilege-escalation-via-lsup-sh-auto-update"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-104474", "GHSA-4qqw-wg6j-834r"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.09, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2c5ece5f-0c70-3948-8283-ad8948ee8324", "product": {"name": "OpenLiteSpeed", "vendor": {"name": "LiteSpeed Technologies"}}, "product_version": "0 <1.9.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "617b90b8-6a2c-32e3-a87e-a90f525c4a2f", "vendor": {"name": "litespeedtech"}}], "isExploited": false}